{"step_index":347,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T10:08:59Z","thinking":"**Analyzing Subnet Connectivity**\n\nThe identified hosts, `th2-revproxyp-fe1` and `th2-centprop-be1`, reside in distinct `/29` subnets. Consequently, traffic between them traverses the default gateway of the source subnet.\n\nThe addition of an `onlink` route is not possible within this configuration.\n\n\n**Understanding Network Redirection**\n\nThe successful `curl` to `172.30.198.33:9443` confirms routing between the subnets. Failure with `109.62.64.18` suggests a routing or DNAT issue. The user's statement about `109.62.64.18:9443` redirecting to `172.30.198.50` demands clarification: is this firewall DNAT or a web UI configuration? The configuration discrepancy between `172.30.198.33` (reverse proxy) and `172.30.198.50` (Map) requires investigation.\n\n\n**Exploring Network Redirection Alternatives**\n\nAdding the route `109.62.64.18/32` via `172.30.198.33` fails because the gateway must be within the local subnet; the correct gateway for the `/29` subnet is `172.30.198.54`. However, direct forwarding to `172.30.198.33` isn't possible, requiring a different approach.\n\nOne method is to use a forwarding utility like `socat`, or similar proxy/tunnel tools to listen on the loopback interface for connections to `109.62.64.18:9443` and forward them to `172.30.198.33:9443`. This involves assigning `109.62.64.18/32` to the loopback interface on the proxy host. This allows any local connection to `109.62.64.18:9443` to be redirected to the internal server.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"~/.ansible/kssh -u superuser 172.30.198.49 '\\ngrep -rn \\\"109.62.64.18\\\" /etc/centreon* /etc/httpd/ /var/www/ 2>/dev/null || true\\ngrep -rn \\\"map.extranetclient\\\" /etc/centreon* /etc/httpd/ /var/www/ 2>/dev/null || true\\n'\"","Cwd":"\"/home/koby\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Running command\"","toolSummary":"\"Check Centreon config on 172.30.198.49 for Map URL\""}}]}
